Linking each name to its WoRMS record shows how far the names in the
inventory differ from current taxonomy. WoRMS gives a different accepted name for {{ q03.n }} of the names used in the
article (Table 4). They fall into four groups:

- **{{ q03.valid | Words }} names the article treats as valid.** Examples are *Parazoanthus parasiticus*,
  now *Umimayanthus parasiticus*, and *Corynactis caribbeorum*, now *Pseudocorynactis
  caribbeorum*.
- **{{ q03.invalid | Words }} names the article already marks as invalid.**
- **{{ q03.label | Words }} old museum labels** that the authors themselves re-identified. One
  of them, *Aiptasia pallida*, is recorded by WoRMS as moved to a new genus by
  {{ citet("grajales2014") }}.
- **{{ q03.spelling | Words }} differences of spelling only.**

The inventory remains as published. The graph adds today's view next to it, with the date on
which it was taken.

